{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLGqtiyRBEWXZWwp2fES","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed this. `trigsimp(1/2*(-I*exp(I*k) + I*exp(-I*k)))` now returns `sin(k)`. For the second example, `trigsimp(f/k)` returns `sin(k)/k`, and adding `.rewrite(sinc)` turns that into `sinc(k)`. `trigsimp` won't write `sinc` on its own; you have to ask for the rewrite.\n\n**What I changed:**\n1. **`sympy/simplify/trigsimp.py`, `trigsimp`:** with the default method, `trigsimp` now also runs `exptrigsimp` on the result when it still contains `exp`. Before, the default path never touched exponentials at all. I put this step after the normal trig simplification on purpose. Running it first broke an existing test: `cot(2)*cos(3)*exp(2)*tan(2)` came out with `exp(2)` turned into `sinh(2) + cosh(2)`.\n2. **`sympy/simplify/trigsimp.py`, `exptrigsimp`:** it now pulls out common factors first (`factor_terms`). That exposes `-exp(I*k) + exp(-I*k)` as its own sum, which it already knew how to turn into `-2*I*sin(k)`. Without this, the `I/2` factor sat inside each term and the pattern was missed. As a result, calling `exptrigsimp` directly on the issue's expression also gives `sin(k)` now.\n3. **`sympy/functions/elementary/trigonometric.py`:** I added `sin(x).rewrite(sinc)`, which gives `x*sinc(x)`. The reverse, `sinc` to `sin`, already worked.\n\n**Tests:** in `test_trigsimp.py`, `test_fu.py`, `test_trigonometric.py` and `test_simplify.py`, 148 tests pass and 4 fail. The same 4 fail on the untouched code: `test_issue_6811_fail`, `test_sin_cos_with_infinity`, `test_factorial_simplify` and `test_simplify_float_vs_integer`. The hyperbolic function tests and the doctests in both changed files pass."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":468,"cache_read_input_tokens":37417,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":468},"output_tokens":723,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9626fc62-256e-4c7b-8738-903c6e989c12","uuid":"ad25d7d4-f721-4791-8fc8-7894a9c50dcd","timestamp":"2026-11-23T17:43:29.911Z","request_id":"req_011ChLGqtZnyY41FBm3cjBin"}
